{
  "format": "srwb",
  "version": "1.0",
  "notebook": {
    "name": "Prolog Generates Lua: Compiler Demo",
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "# Prolog Generates Lua\n\nThis workbook demonstrates UnifyWeaver compiling Prolog predicates into **Lua** code.\n\nThe workflow:\n1. Define Prolog predicates (facts + rules)\n2. UnifyWeaver detects the recursion pattern (transitive closure)\n3. The compiler generates idiomatic Lua with tables and BFS traversal\n4. Execute the generated Lua code in the Lua kernel\n\n**Requires:** Install the UnifyWeaver package first (Browse Packages).\n\n**Limitation:** Lua variables don't persist across cells. The generated code includes a CLI entry point that reads from stdin — in the notebook we can't use stdin, so we seed facts and queries manually in a separate cell.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Load UnifyWeaver compiler modules\n['../init'].\n:- use_module(unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "load_compiler"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Define a family tree as Prolog facts\n:- dynamic parent/2, ancestor/2.\n\nparent(alice, bob).\nparent(bob, charlie).\nparent(bob, diana).\nparent(charlie, eve).\nparent(diana, frank).\n\n% Transitive closure: ancestor(X, Y) if X is an ancestor of Y\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Y).\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Z), ancestor(Z, Y).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "family_tree"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Compile ancestor/2 to Lua — write raw generated code to cell\nrecursive_compiler:compile_recursive(ancestor/2, [target(lua)], Code),\nuser:nb_write('lua_generated', '.code', Code),\nwriteln('Lua code written to cell: lua_generated').",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "compile_to_lua"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "## Generated Lua Code\n\nThe cell below shows the generated Lua code. It includes a CLI section\nthat reads from stdin — this won't work in the notebook, so the next cell\nseeds the facts and runs queries directly.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "-- This cell will be populated by the compiler.\n-- Run the 'compile_to_lua' cell above first.",
        "language": "lua",
        "name": "lua_generated"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "## Run Queries\n\nThe cell below seeds the family tree facts manually and runs ancestor queries.\nThis is separate because the generated code's stdin-based CLI doesn't work in-browser.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "-- Seed facts and query (standalone — doesn't depend on generated cell)\nlocal rel = {}\nlocal function add_fact(from, to)\n    if not rel[from] then rel[from] = {} end\n    table.insert(rel[from], to)\nend\nlocal function find_all(start)\n    local results = {}\n    local visited = { [start] = true }\n    local queue = { start }\n    local qi = 1\n    while qi <= #queue do\n        local current = queue[qi]\n        qi = qi + 1\n        for _, next_node in ipairs(rel[current] or {}) do\n            if not visited[next_node] then\n                visited[next_node] = true\n                table.insert(queue, next_node)\n                table.insert(results, next_node)\n            end\n        end\n    end\n    return results\nend\nlocal function check(start, target)\n    for _, v in ipairs(find_all(start)) do\n        if v == target then return true end\n    end\n    return false\nend\n\nadd_fact(\"alice\", \"bob\")\nadd_fact(\"bob\", \"charlie\")\nadd_fact(\"bob\", \"diana\")\nadd_fact(\"charlie\", \"eve\")\nadd_fact(\"diana\", \"frank\")\n\nlocal results = find_all(\"alice\")\nprint(\"Descendants of alice: \" .. table.concat(results, \", \"))\nprint(\"alice -> eve: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"eve\")))\nprint(\"alice -> frank: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"frank\")))",
        "language": "lua",
        "name": "lua_queries"
      }
    ]
  }
}
